# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository.
#
# This exists because of a silent failure mode: a CRLF line ending inside a
# frontmatter value makes Jekyll read `image: images/people/ryan-eng.jpg\r`,
# which matches no file on disk, so the portrait falls back to
# images/fallback.svg and no thumbnail is generated. Nothing warns — the page
# just shows the placeholder. Four member pages were broken this way.
#
# text=auto lets git decide what is text, and eol=lf stores it with Unix
# endings regardless of the editor that wrote it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Portraits and other binaries must never be line-ending converted.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
